{"author":"Joe Oakhart","author_email":"joeoakhart@navapbc.com","data":{"alias":"longish-ripe-snowyowl","creation_channel":"python","description":"## Context\n\nAn external four-arm plan-review benchmark judged rebar's findings alongside three other\nreviewers (Compound Engineering, superpowers, mini-swe-agent) on two third-party plans. Three\nindependent classifiers per run, majority-aggregated, Fleiss kappa 0.856 and 0.900, zero\ncontested items.\n\nrebar was the ONLY arm whose row count exceeded its distinct-issue count. Across the two runs it\nemitted 35 findings covering 29 distinct issues (+21%). Every other arm netted zero or negative\ninflation, meaning judges split their rows into more issues than the arm claimed, not fewer.\n\nThis reproduces a Wave 1 observation (+49 net merged rows study-wide) on clean input: both plans\ncarried their own verbatim acceptance criteria, no harness scaffolding was added, every arm read\nbyte-identical input, and all four ran concurrently. So input asymmetry and scaffolding are ruled\nout as explanations.\n\n## Observed instances\n\nFive groups where two or more rebar findings were judged to state the SAME issue.\n\n### carbon (ts-carbon-dsx-card-web-component), 3 groups, 5 net duplicate rows\n\n**Group A — absent shared card SCSS. FOUR rebar rows for one issue.**\n\n| ballot | finding id | criteria | band | priority | block_threshold | tier |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 2 | fac2282ff04867c07 | E4 | blocking | 0.8 | 0.75 | LLM |\n| 4 | f73a2ac0bd5912fa0 | G1G2 | blocking | 0.8 | 0.70 | LLM |\n| 7 | fae54d7542a904816 | T1 | blocking | 0.8 | 0.70 | LLM |\n| 8 | f7cb2731aec88a265 | T3 | advisory | 0.8 | 0.90 | LLM |\n\nAll four assert the same fact: the plan claims `packages/styles/scss/components/card/_card.scss`\nalready exists; it does not exist at the pinned SHA. Three of the four are BLOCKING.\n\n**Group B — absent React Card referent. Two rows.**\n\n| ballot | finding id | criteria | band | priority | block_threshold |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 3 | f036b5d8ba8ce1922 | E4 | blocking | 0.8 | 0.75 |\n| 5 | f5677bcc33d08f796 | G1G2 | blocking | 0.8 | 0.70 |\n\nBoth blocking.\n\n**Group C — Lit context file location contradictory. Two rows.**\n\n| ballot | finding id | criteria | band | priority | block_threshold |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 9 | fafd331051f282d48 | A1 | advisory | 0.68 | 0.95 |\n| 10 | fce6a492c25ad79d8 | G1G2 | advisory | 0.68 | 0.70 |\n\nBoth advisory.\n\n### uswds (scss-uswds-elements-dsx-token-migration), 2 groups, 2 net duplicate rows\n\n**Group D — #302's required CSV input does not exist. Two rows, both blocking.**\n\n| ballot | finding id | criteria | band | priority | block_threshold | cohort |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | fa397c3a9c775bb37 | E2 | blocking | 1.0 | 0.60 | COH, E1, E2, E6, F1, T5d |\n| 6 | f2fe1f5b397e2040f | G1G2 | blocking | 0.9 | 0.70 | G1G2 |\n\n**Group E — no sub-issue owns the prepare-script rewrite. Two rows, both blocking.**\n\n| ballot | finding id | criteria | band | priority | block_threshold | cohort |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 3 | f8fbdb6fdf4b8abc3 | COH, E6 | blocking | 0.8889 | 0.60 | COH, E1, E2, E6, F1, T5d |\n| 8 | f164935f57c7fe71a | G6 | blocking | 0.8 | 0.60 | G6 |\n\n## Fingerprints\n\n**No two members of any group share a finding id.** All 12 duplicate rows carry distinct ids.\nAny dedup keyed on the `id` field would therefore not have collapsed any of these.\n\n**Separately, one id IS stable across two different plans.** `f607dd457c67f9209` appears in both\nruns, in both cases with `criteria: [\"P6\"]`, `tier: DET`, and the identical generic text\n\"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.\" The two plans are unrelated\nthird-party documents in different repositories and languages. Recorded as an observation about\nid stability, not as a claim about its cause.\n\n## Criteria pattern\n\nDuplicate members always originate from DIFFERENT criteria; no group contains two rows from the\nsame criterion. `G1G2` is a member of four of the five groups. `E4` appears in two. All twelve\nduplicate rows are `tier: LLM`; the `tier: DET` findings observed (P4, P6) were singletons.\n\nIn two groups the `cohort` field differs between members that state the same issue: one member\ncarries a multi-criterion cohort (`COH, E1, E2, E6, F1, T5d`) while its partner carries a\nsingle-criterion cohort (`G1G2`, `G6`).\n\n## Were duplicates dropped, and were they blocking?\n\n**Not dropped.** Each run dropped exactly one finding (carbon `faebc723ce13f9e41`, criteria T5e;\nuswds `f83c75f75085873a2`, criteria T7), both at priority 0.0 against a 0.95 threshold. Neither\nis a duplicate: lexical overlap with the nearest surviving finding is 0.10 and 0.067\nrespectively. `overflow` and `indeterminate` are empty on both runs. So every duplicate survived\ninto the verdict.\n\n**Mostly blocking.** Four of the five groups contain two or more BLOCKING members. Group A\nblocks three times for one defect. Consequence: an operator reading the verdict sees the same\ndefect counted repeatedly against the block decision, and a reader counting blocking findings\noverstates the number of distinct blocking defects.\n\n## Reproduction material\n\n- Verdicts: `wave3/rebar-runs/{ts-carbon-dsx-card-web-component,scss-uswds-elements-dsx-token-migration}.verdict.json`\n- Adjudications with per-issue membership: `artifacts/adjudications/<run>.adjudication.json`,\n  key `merged_issues`; per-arm totals under `arms.rebar` (`total_findings`, `distinct_issues`,\n  `same_arm_merges`).\n- Ballots: `artifacts/ballots/<run>.ballot.json` (item -> `arm_finding_id` mapping).\n- All in the external study directory, not in this repository.\n\n## Not claimed here\n\nNo root cause is proposed. This ticket deliberately reports observations only: which rows\nduplicated, their criteria, ids, bands, priorities, thresholds, tiers and cohorts, whether ids\nmatched, whether anything was dropped, and whether duplicates were blocking. Determining why\nseveral criteria independently emit one issue, and whether that is intended behaviour with a\nmissing merge step or unintended overlap in criteria scope, is left to the investigator.","id":"2331-3e0e-f880-4837","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Plan review emits one issue as several findings under different criteria; duplicates are blocking and none are deduplicated"},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1789449200047063001,"uuid":"6dd13185-a179-4cef-85fd-7862fb48a4a3"}